{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Despised and accounted not among men.</b> He ceased to be counted among men." "<b>A man of pains.</b> The servant of HaShem. And if it applies to all, the meaning is like איש מלחמה (man of war), and it is close to the meaning of a noun, and it is in construct state, and the meaning of מכאובות וחלי (pains and sickness) is the distress of exile." "<b>And as one hiding faces from him.</b> There is to this day a nation that, when it sees a Jew, hides its face from him. And the meaning is that it does not look at him to save him."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 53, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:15.964201078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}